## Context

Child of tracking ticket 0251. The author ratified Option A
(skill-invokes-skill): `/hunt` is the single canonical ticket-execution
core, and every path must invoke it mechanically. `skills/raid/SKILL.md`
Phase 5 currently says "Each agent follows `/hunt` workflow" — a prose
paraphrase, not an invocation. A paraphrase is exactly what drifted
between the aedist Wave A and Wave B prompts (2026-06-11/12): the
execution contract lived in prompt-writing memory instead of the
versioned SKILL.md.

## Relevant files
- `skills/raid/SKILL.md` — Phase 5 (Execute), ~line 153-163
- `docs/imagine-0251-entry-points-2026-07-12.md` — design note, Option A

## Actions
1. Rewrite Phase 5 so the execute agent's FIRST action is an imperative,
   greppable instruction to invoke the hunt skill with the ticket ID —
   `Skill(skill: "hunt", args: "<id>")` — not a description of what hunt
   does.
2. State explicitly that the agent prompt must not paraphrase or inline
   the hunt steps; the skill loader supplies the live contract.

## Test
- Extend the skills adherence/hygiene test (or add one) asserting
  `skills/raid/SKILL.md` contains the imperative Skill-invocation string
  and no longer the prose "follows `/hunt` workflow" phrasing.

## Verification
- [ ] Phase 5 opens the agent contract with the mechanical invocation
- [ ] Test proves RED on the pre-fix text, GREEN after

## Invariants
- Raid's wave grouping, model policy, and verify/merge phases unchanged
- Entry-point count stays at 2 (hunt, raid)

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Phase 5 instructs `Skill(hunt)` imperatively
- [ ] Guard test in place
- [ ] `make check` passes
